{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-62467-r4515901","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Bran Muffins","sourcePageId":62467,"sourceRevision":"4515901","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2025-06-19T22:55:42Z","sourceRevisionUser":"Kittycataclysm","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Bran%20Muffins&oldid=4515901","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T12:24:45.135Z","sourceCategories":["Category:Baking recipes","Category:Breakfast recipes","Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes for muffins","Category:Recipes using all-purpose flour","Category:Recipes using baking powder","Category:Recipes using baking soda","Category:Recipes using bran","Category:Recipes using brown sugar","Category:Recipes using buttermilk","Category:Recipes using egg","Category:Recipes using margarine","Category:Recipes with metric units","Category:Very Easy recipes"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"e6d01850b13eacf0a32cd9883008e1ed697234059a1e4634d6d5fcc211747c24","sourceWikitext":"__NOTOC__\n{{recipesummary|category=Muffin recipes|servings=12|time=20–25 minutes|difficulty=1\n}}\n\n{{recipe}} | [[Cookbook:Bread|Bread]] | [[Cookbook:Breakfast Recipes|Breakfast Recipes]]\n\nA delicious '''bran muffin''' recipe that makes an excellent [[Cookbook:Breakfast Recipes|breakfast]].\n\n==Ingredients==\n\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Cup|cup]] (240 [[Cookbook:Milliliter|ml]]) natural [[Cookbook:Wheat Bran|wheat bran]]\n* ¾ [[Cookbook:Cup|cup]] (180 ml) cultured [[Cookbook:Buttermilk|buttermilk]]\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Egg|egg]]\n* 2 [[Cookbook:Tablespoon|tablespoons]] [[Cookbook:Margarine|margarine]]\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Cup|cup]] (240 ml) [[Cookbook:Flour|all-purpose flour]]\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|teaspoon]] [[Cookbook:Baking Powder|baking powder]]\n* ½ [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|teaspoon]] [[Cookbook:Baking Soda|baking soda]]\n* ½ [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|teaspoon]] [[Cookbook:Salt|salt]]\n* ½ [[Cookbook:Cup|cup]] (120 ml) [[Cookbook:Brown Sugar|brown sugar]]\n\n== Equipment ==\n\n* [[Cookbook:Mixing Bowl|Mixing bowl]]\n* [[Cookbook:Muffin Pan|Muffin cups]], greased or lined\n* [[Cookbook:Measuring Cup|Measuring cup]]\n* [[Cookbook:Oven|Oven]]\n\n==Procedure==\n#Stir wheat bran and buttermilk together in a [[Cookbook:Mixing Bowl|mixing bowl]].\n#[[Cookbook:Creaming|Cream]] together egg, brown sugar and margarine in another mixing bowl. \n#Combine remaining ingredients in a third bowl. Add to [[Cookbook:Batter|batter]], and stir just to moisten.\n#Fill muffin cups ¾ full.\n#Bake at [[Cookbook:Oven temperatures|400°F]] (200°C) for 15 to 20 minutes.\n\n==Notes, tips, and variations==\n*For bran raisin muffins, add 1 [[Cookbook:Cup|cup]] [[Cookbook:Raisin|raisins]].\n*If you do not want to buy store-bought cultured buttermilk, you can make your own by adding 1 [[Cookbook:Tablespoon|tablespoon]] [[Cookbook:Lemon Juice|lemon juice]] or [[Cookbook:Vinegar|vinegar]] to 1 [[Cookbook:Cup|cup]] of [[Cookbook:Milk|milk]]. Let it sit for five minutes before using.\n*Tastes best when still warm.\n\n[[Category:Recipes using bran]]\n[[Category:Recipes for muffins]]\n[[Category:Baking recipes]]\n[[Category:Breakfast recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes_with_metric_units]]\n[[Category:Recipes using baking powder]]\n[[Category:Recipes using baking soda]]\n[[Category:Recipes using brown sugar]]\n[[Category: